WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.840
When you expand your business to an Amazon marketplace outside your home country, you'll need

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.366
to understand your importing and exporting obligations as a non-resident seller.

00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:18.120
In this

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.080
video, we'll go over how you can get started with shipping your products to Canada, either

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.688
to an Amazon Fulfillment Center using FBA or directly to the customer.

00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:28.840
This would include

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.820
working with a logistics provider such as a customs broker or freight forwarder, becoming

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.624
a non-resident importer, and preparing a commercial invoice.

00:00:37.624 --> 00:00:40.160
This information will be most relevant

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:46.800
to sellers shipping from the US into Canada, but may also help sellers in other countries.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.880
You'll notice through your unified account that your current listings are not automatically

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.461
created on both Amazon.

00:00:52.461 --> 00:00:53.647
com and Amazon.

00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:54.042
ca.

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:57.205
You'll need to add your items to Amazon.

00:00:57.205 --> 00:00:57.600
ca

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.784
just like you did when you first listed them on Amazon.

00:01:00.784 --> 00:01:01.073
com.

00:01:01.073 --> 00:01:02.520
For more information on this

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:08.488
process, please watch our Seller university video adding listings to Amazon.

00:01:08.488 --> 00:01:10.115
ca and Amazon.

00:01:10.115 --> 00:01:10.658
com.

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:11.200
mx.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.840
Once your listings are created in Canada, you'll have to find a way to fulfill your orders,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.840
whether it's by shipping your items to a Fulfillment Center or directly to the customer.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.800
If your business is located outside of Canada, you'll need to become a non-resident importer

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:32.680
or NRI to ensure all deliveries to Canadian residents are delivery duty paid or DDP, and

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.054
that you or a broker acts as the importer of record or IOR.

00:01:37.054 --> 00:01:38.400
Customs brokers or freight

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.040
forwarders can provide further guidance on getting an NRI and registering for a Canadian

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:43.728
business number.

00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:46.480
Along with the NRI, you'll need to obtain

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.280
a Canadian business number, which has 15 characters, 9 numbers to identify the business,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.654
plus 2 letters and 4 numbers to identify the program and each account.

00:01:56.654 --> 00:01:58.000
This must be obtained

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.712
prior to the first importation.

00:01:59.712 --> 00:02:03.480
If you are collecting tax on your sales in Canada, you

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:09.520
are required to register for goods and services tax or harmonized sales tax in Canada and

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.160
remit the amount that is over and above what you originally paid out.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.000
We recommend reaching

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.341
out to a tax advisor for all tax related questions.

00:02:17.341 --> 00:02:19.680
In the seller central help section, search

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.352
for "Canada Tax and Regulatory Considerations" for more details.

00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:25.800
Amazon will not act as the

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.400
importer of record for any shipment and if you leave this field blank, your shipment

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.798
may be refused or returned to you.

00:02:32.798 --> 00:02:35.880
The importer of record ensures all shipments have delivery

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.504
duties filed and paid and that they are compliant with all local laws and regulations.

00:02:40.504 --> 00:02:41.120
The most

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.520
common reason shipments are refused is because delivery duties are not paid, so please make

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:50.045
sure to confirm with your carrier to avoid any issues.

00:02:50.045 --> 00:02:52.160
Also, there are certain items that

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.600
are prohibited or restricted.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.840
Make sure to double check applicable laws and regulations

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.360
including health Canada regulations and FBA policies before moving forward.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.200
Once you've chosen a shipping company and are ready to ship your goods, the shipper will

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.714
prepare the commercial invoice.

00:03:07.714 --> 00:03:11.120
It's critical the commercial invoice is accurate to avoid

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.260
delays clearing customs.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.440
If you are shipping to an Amazon fulfillment center, enter the

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.920
fulfillment center name in the "in care of" and then the fulfillment center address in

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.800
the "ship to address" field.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.560
Include a detailed description of the goods being invoiced including

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:33.320
customs harmonized codes, the number of units, unit values and the total of value of each

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:33.668
product.

00:03:33.668 --> 00:03:38.880
For samples or products with no commercial value, you'll still need to state a nominal

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.522
or fair market value for customs purposes.

00:03:41.522 --> 00:03:44.920
For terms of sale, the shipper or FBA seller

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.680
should pay all applicable duty and taxes and will be responsible for clearing customs

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.911
before delivery to the Amazon fulfillment center.

00:03:52.911 --> 00:03:55.680
Sellers are not authorized to import

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.280
goods in Amazon's name or show Amazon as the declarant or importer of record on the

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.775
customs entry documentation.

00:04:01.775 --> 00:04:05.760
For shipments to Amazon fulfillment centers, include the

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.080
Amazon FBA shipment ID that you receive when you create the shipment in Seller Central.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:15.680
The shipment tracking number can also be an airway bill number if you're using a carrier

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.813
such as FedEx or UPS.

00:04:17.813 --> 00:04:22.080
You are responsible for determining whether any taxes apply to

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.619
your business and accounting for those taxes.

00:04:24.619 --> 00:04:27.520
Please consult with the tax advisor to understand

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.960
your obligations in Canada.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.920
Now that you're ready to ship into Canada, you should also

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.589
be aware of how to handle returns.

00:04:35.589 --> 00:04:38.640
When processing an international return for orders, sellers

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.955
must use one of the following methods.

00:04:40.955 --> 00:04:43.600
One, sellers could provide the customer with a

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:50.000
prepaid return mailing label to have the item returned to an international location or two.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.382
Sellers could provide a local return address in Canada or three.

00:04:53.382 --> 00:04:54.920
Sellers could offer a full

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:58.040
refund without requesting the item to be returned.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.160
FBA items that are still in sellable condition

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:06.080
can be returned to FBA and will automatically be back online once they're returned and checked

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:06.416
in.

00:05:06.416 --> 00:05:11.800
Items that are defective or otherwise need to be removed from FBA can only be shipped

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.680
from an FBA facility to a Canadian address.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.560
If you're based outside of Canada and need

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:22.336
to remove an item from your FBA Canada inventory, be aware that the Amazon.

00:05:22.336 --> 00:05:23.360
ca removal service

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:28.640
will only ship to domestic Canadian addresses and is currently unable to return inventory

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.405
to an address outside of Canada.

00:05:30.405 --> 00:05:33.640
You may want to work with a freight forwarding company to

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.992
move your exports out of Canada.

00:05:35.992 --> 00:05:37.952
Thank you for joining us.

00:05:37.952 --> 00:05:39.520
For more information, search

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.688
North America Unified Account in Seller Central Help.

00:05:42.688 --> 00:05:43.480
Happy selling!
